# EvenShock is served from https://ftable.co.il/evenshock/, a subdirectory of a
# site that sends its own Content-Security-Policy. That policy's connect-src
# allowlists ftable's Supabase project, not ours, so the browser refuses every
# request to ours and wallet sign-in never gets to run:
#
#   Refused to connect to 'https://qgnxppzchqwpwerajhlu.supabase.co/...'
#   because it violates the document's Content Security Policy.
#
# This file confines the fix to this directory; the parent site is untouched.
# Vite copies public/ into dist/, and the FTP deploy ships dist/, so it lands
# next to index.html with no manual server step.

<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  # `edit`, not `set`. `set` replaces the whole header, which would silently drop
  # every other directive the parent policy carries -- script-src,
  # frame-ancestors, object-src and the rest -- trading a connection bug for a
  # materially weaker page. `edit` rewrites only the connect-src directive and
  # leaves the others exactly as the parent set them.
  #
  # Both forms are listed because we cannot see how the parent sets the header:
  # plain `edit` reaches headers on successful responses, `always edit` reaches
  # the table used by `Header always set` and by error responses. Whichever does
  # not match is a harmless no-op.
  #
  # The replacement list is deliberately minimal rather than the parent's list
  # plus ours. Inside /evenshock/ nothing loads from cdn.jsdelivr.net, from
  # ftable's Supabase project, or from its analytics hosts -- this app's only
  # external origin is its own Supabase project -- so re-listing them would
  # widen this directory's policy for no reason.
  #
  # wss:// is not optional. Supabase Realtime opens a websocket, and a policy
  # allowing only https:// blocks it. Leaving it out would surface later as
  # multiplayer failing rather than as a sign-in failure, which is a much harder
  # bug to find.
  Header        edit Content-Security-Policy "connect-src[^;]*" "connect-src 'self' https://qgnxppzchqwpwerajhlu.supabase.co wss://qgnxppzchqwpwerajhlu.supabase.co https://api.devnet.solana.com"
  Header always edit Content-Security-Policy "connect-src[^;]*" "connect-src 'self' https://qgnxppzchqwpwerajhlu.supabase.co wss://qgnxppzchqwpwerajhlu.supabase.co https://api.devnet.solana.com"
</IfModule>

# The <IfModule> guard is load-bearing. An unguarded Header directive on a host
# without mod_headers is a fatal .htaccess error, which would turn "the app
# cannot reach Supabase" into "the whole directory returns 500". Guarded, the
# worst case is that nothing changes and the original console error remains --
# which is also how you tell mod_headers is unavailable.
